@startuml possession-flow
title Possession Resolution (§3.2–§3.5, §3.7 blocks, §3.8 missed-shot OOB,\n§3.9 turnover causes, §3.10 rebounding fouls + bonus, §3.11 and-1)

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start

note right
  **§3.4 coach pace** scales the possession COUNT
  (loop bound), blended across both coaches.
end note

partition "RotationState — between-possession sub (§3.5)" {
  :drain on-floor energy (× endurance)
  recover benched energy;
  :force off any fouled-out player
  //getFouls() >= FOUL_OUT_LIMIT// → sub from full roster;
  :fatigue sub — pull most-tired starter below
  //subAggressiveness// threshold for freshest bench
  within //rotationDepth//; starters pulled later / return first;
  note right
    Deterministic given (energy, fouls, coach attrs).
    **Consumes no RNG, emits no events.** onFloor()
    is always exactly 5 (least-fouled stays as last resort).
  end note
}

repeat
:ShotSelector
  pick shooter (offensive-weight draw)
  pick shot type (skill-weight draw
  //× offensiveScheme shot-mix lean §3.4//);

partition "TurnoverResolver (§3.9 causes — decisions.md #027)" {
  if (turnover?\n//ballSecurity vs stealing/individualDefense//\n//× defensiveScheme pressure §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    note right
      **The gate above is UNCHANGED by §3.9** (#027 A) — a turnover
      happens exactly as often as before. Only AFTER a turnover is
      declared does a weighted draw pick WHICH of NINE causes it was,
      so the draw re-partitions the label without moving the count.
      That is what made §3.9 free by construction.
      Leans (#027 C): SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION on //acumen//↓ ×
      //defensiveScheme//↑; OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS on //teamOffense//↓.
      STOLEN stays dominant. Every cause charges the ball-handler.
    end note
    if (cause == STOLEN?\n//weighted nine-way draw//) then (yes)
      :TURNOVER — STOLEN
      credit defender steal;
    else (no)
      :TURNOVER — one of
      SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION / OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS /
      TRAVELLING / LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS / 3_SECONDS_VIOLATION /
      8_SECONDS_BACKCOURT_VIOLATION / OVER_AND_BACK
      //no stealer credited//;
    endif
    stop
  endif
}

partition "FoulResolver" {
  if (DRIVE or POST?) then (yes)
    if (foul?\n//foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — SHOOTING_FOUL
      charge defender foul;
      note right
        foul rate × defensiveScheme pressure §3.4.
        This is the **pre-shot** foul — the shot is stopped,
        a 2-FT trip, mutually exclusive with a made basket.
        The **and-1** (foul WITH a made shot) is a separate
        post-make roll (§3.11, inside SHOT — MADE below).
      end note

      repeat
        if (free throw made?\n//freeThrows skill//) then (yes)
          :FREE_THROW — MADE_SHOOTING (source-tagged §3.11 D)
          +1 point;
        else (no)
          :FREE_THROW — MISSED_SHOOTING;
        endif
      repeat while (FREE_THROWS_PER_FOUL done?) is (no) not (yes)
      stop
    endif
  endif
}

partition "ShotResolver" {
  :record FGA (+ 3PA if THREE);

  if (BLOCKED? //§3.7 — decisions.md #025//\n//P(BLOCK) carved off the top (A1), then MAKE/MISS on remainder//\n//contest: defender rimProtection (rim) / shotContest (jumper)//\n//vs shooter finishing (B2); own BLOCK_SENSITIVITY, THREE very-low (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :SHOT — BLOCKED_*
    event: PlayType.SHOT, outcome BLOCKED_* (F1)
    primaryPlayerId = shooter (the victim)
    shooter charged missed FGA (+3PA if THREE), 0 FGM (F3)
    blocker.recordBlock() — separate credit, not on event (F2)
    no assistPlayerId (F4);
    note right
      **Block = a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a
      turnover outcome** (§3.2: TURNOVER/STOLEN + recordSteal).
      v3: one three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw — no double-count
      (probs sum to 1). No new PlayType.BLOCK. Reconciliation:
      count(SHOT outcome LIKE 'BLOCKED%') == sum(BoxScore.blocks).
    end note

    partition "BlockResolver (§3.7 — #025 D)" {
      note right
        A blocked ball is a **chaotic loose ball**, NOT the
        offenseRebound-vs-defenseRebound box-out contest — so
        recovery is a FLAT four-way roll (fixed weights, same
        for every block, defense-leaning). Weights are
        placeholders → calibrate empirically (~5 blocks/team).
      end note
      switch (recovery? //flat four-way roll (D)//)
      case (RECOVERED_OFFENSE)
        :in-bounds, offense retains
        → second-chance;
        stop
      case (RECOVERED_DEFENSE)
        :in-bounds, defense's ball
        → possession over;
        stop
      case (OOB_OFFENSE)
        :OOB off the blocker
        → offense retains → second-chance;
        stop
      case (OOB_DEFENSE)
        :OOB off the shooter
        → defense's ball → possession over;
        stop
      endswitch
    }
  else (no)
    if (shot made?\n//offense skill vs defense skill//\n//× acumen + teamOffense/teamDefense §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
      :SHOT — MADE_*
      +2 or +3 points;
      partition "Assist (§3.4)" {
        if (assisted?\n//supporting-cast passing draw//) then (yes)
          :stamp assist_player_id
          credit assister;
        endif
      }
      partition "And-1 (§3.11 — decisions.md #029)" {
        note right
          **And-1 = a SECOND, post-make foul roll** (A1), carved
          BESIDE the assist — the pre-shot foul branch + BASE_FOUL
          are untouched, so this rate is independently tunable
          (the §3.7 block / §3.10 rebound-foul carve, a third time).
          A made basket already ended the possession → the and-1
          NEVER forks it; it only tacks on ONE FT (B). Coexists with
          the assist, doesn't interact (A3). Rate = rareEventProbability
          on AND_ONE_BASE + its own AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C).
        end note
        if (DRIVE or POST? //A2 — §3.12 widens to all shot types//) then (yes)
          if (and-1?\n//shooter foulDrawing vs defender discipline//\n//× defensivePressure; AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
            :FOUL — AND_ONE
            charge defender foul (feeds foul-outs + §3.10 tally)
            committing_team_id = defTeamId (reuses #028 D column);
            :FREE_THROW — *_AND_ONE (source-tagged, D)
            ONE FT for the shooter (AND_ONE_FREE_THROWS = 1, B)
            +1 if made; FG points already recorded;
          endif
        endif
      }
      stop
    else (no)
      :SHOT — MISSED_*;
    endif
  endif
}

partition "Rebounding foul (§3.10 — decisions.md #028)" {
  note right
    **Carved off the TOP of the rebound phase** (C) — rolled BEFORE
    the board contest and SHORT-CIRCUITING it on a hit (the whistle
    stopped play, so nobody rebounds). Same shape as §3.7's block
    carve, which keeps this rate independently tunable — it never
    entangles with the rebound weights.
    **TWO-SIDED** (A2): a defensive box-out push (dominant) or an
    offensive over-the-back (the minority). The committer is drawn
    //foulProne//-weighted from the committing five, so the
    undisciplined bang bodies commit most of them.
    Rate = rareEventProbability(REBOUND_FOUL_BASE, …,
    REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY) × defensivePressure — floor-free,
    its own dial (the PROB_FLOOR trap, #028 impl note).
  end note
  if (rebounding foul?\n//aggregate foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× defensivePressure; REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — REBOUNDING_FOUL_DEFENSE or _OFFENSE
    charge committer foul (feeds foul-outs §3.5)
    committing_team_id = the committing side (#028 D);
    note right
      **EMIT-THEN-COUNT** (A1, the crux): the FOUL event is written
      FIRST, then GameData.isInBonus(committingTeam, period) reads
      the log — so the Nth foul (reaching BONUS_FOULS_PER_PERIOD = 5)
      **itself** sends the fouled team to the line. The penalty is
      **DERIVED from the FOUL events, never stored** — no teamFouls
      field, no reset logic (the #023-F / #013 / #015 discipline).
    end note
    if (committing team in the bonus?\n//count(FOUL by team, period) >= 5//) then (yes)
      :FREE_THROW ×2 — *_BONUS (source-tagged §3.11 D)
      the FOULED team shoots (foulDrawing-weighted shooter)
      → possession over either way;
      stop
    else (no)
      if (DEFENSE committed?) then (yes)
        :offense was fouled → RETAINS
        → second-chance (respects the off-rebound cap);
        stop
      else (no — offense committed)
        :over-the-back → defense's ball
        → possession over;
        stop
      endif
    endif
  endif
}

partition "MissedShotResolver (§3.8 — #026) — wraps ReboundResolver (§3.3)" {
  note right
    **§3.8 (#026 A/B):** a missed shot resolves to ONE of FOUR
    outcomes in a single SKILL-WEIGHTED draw. MissedShotResolver
    WRAPS ReboundResolver (unchanged) for the rebound-vs-rebound
    balance, then applies a fixed DEFENSE-LEANING lean to carve
    the two OOB slices. NOT a separate "is it OOB?" sub-decision.
    OOB credits NO rebounder (#026 E) and must stay out of the
    rebound reconciliation. Skill-weighted here is the deliberate
    difference from §3.7's FLAT BlockResolver (#026 C).
  end note
  :pick offensive rebounder (offenseRebound draw)
  pick defensive rebounder (defenseRebound draw);
  switch (missed-shot outcome?\n//rebound balance: offenseRebound vs defenseRebound//\n//× fatigueFactor §3.5; OOB slices defense-leaning lean §3.8//\n//(offense-retained forced to ending once cap hit)//)
  case (OFFENSIVE rebound)
    :REBOUND — OFFENSIVE
    credit off rebounder
    → offense retains → second-chance;
    stop
  case (DEFENSIVE rebound)
    :REBOUND — DEFENSIVE
    credit def rebounder
    → possession over;
    stop
  case (OOB — offense §3.8)
    :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_OFFENSE (no rebounder)
    → offense retains → second-chance;
    stop
  case (OOB — defense §3.8)
    :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_DEFENSE (no rebounder)
    → possession over;
    stop
  endswitch
}
repeat while (off rebounds < MAX_OFFENSIVE_REBOUNDS_PER_POSSESSION?) is (yes) not (no)

:cap reached → next miss forced to DEFENSIVE rebound;
stop

legend bottom left
  **Probability formula (all resolvers)**
  p = base(path) + SENSITIVITY × (offense − defense) / 10
  Clamped [PROB_FLOOR 0.02, PROB_CEILING 0.97] for
  NORMAL-frequency outcomes (contestProbability).
  Average vs average → base rate. All constants in SimConfig.

  **RARE events use a different clamp** (§3.7 / §3.10 / §3.11)
  rareEventProbability(base, driving, opposing, sensitivity)
  clamps to **[0, ceiling] with NO floor** — on a thin base the
  0.02 floor would act as a FLOOR and make the knob tunable only
  UPWARD (found the hard way in §3.10, #028 impl note). Each rare
  event also carries its OWN sensitivity, far below the global 0.5,
  which would otherwise swamp a thin base: BLOCK_SENSITIVITY 0.12,
  REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY 0.10, AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY 0.10.
  NB a zero base does **not** disable a rare event — the skill term
  alone stays positive off an even contest; only the caller's gate
  (e.g. isContactType) truly switches one off.

  **§3.4 coach / chemistry modifiers** (decisions.md #022)
  Each is the avg-10 deviation multiplier
  m(attr) = 1 + COACH_SENSITIVITY × (attr − 10) / 10
  applied as a thumb on the scale over the contest above.

  **§3.5 fatigue / substitution** (decisions.md #023)
  Between-possession sub (top, RNG-free) changes WHO is on
  the floor; each contest skill is × fatigueFactor(energy),
  ×1.0 at a full tank. Minutes are a possession-share
  projection (no game clock). Foul-out = getFouls() >= 6.

  **§3.7 blocked shots** (decisions.md #025)
  BLOCKED? is one leg of a three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw inside
  ShotResolver (v3): P(BLOCK) carved off the top, defender-vs-
  finisher contest (own BLOCK_SENSITIVITY). A block is a SHOT/
  BLOCKED_* event (a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a
  TURNOVER outcome) — missed FGA on the shooter + a BLK via
  recordBlock() on the defender, no assist. BlockResolver runs a
  flat four-way loose-ball recovery (offense/defense × in-bounds/
  OOB). Recalibrated: ~5 blocks/team, §3.4/§3.5 aggregates held.

  **§3.8 missed-shot OOB** (decisions.md #026)
  A missed shot resolves to ONE of FOUR outcomes in a single
  skill-weighted draw: OFFENSIVE / DEFENSIVE rebound, or OOB
  offense / OOB defense. MissedShotResolver WRAPS ReboundResolver
  (the two-way skill contest, unchanged): it carves the OOB share
  off the top by a flat defense-leaning lean FIRST (skill-
  independent), then runs the board contest only on the clean-
  rebound remainder — NOT a separate OOB sub-decision, so OOB never
  inherits the board winner. Both sail-out (shot flies OOB
  untouched) and tipped-OOB (a board contest, last-touch decides)
  land here, sharing one OOB outcome each (offense/defense). OOB is
  a REBOUND event with an OUT_OF_BOUNDS_* outcome that credits NO
  rebounder and stays out of the rebound reconciliation (#026 E).
  Skill-weighted — the deliberate difference from §3.7's flat
  BlockResolver (#026 C). OOB-offense is a third offense-retention
  path against the one MAX_OFFENSIVE_REBOUNDS cap. Sail-out is a
  new outcome (fewer second chances) → VERIFIED harness-neutral
  (#026 D): OOB ~3/team/game, §3.4/§3.5 aggregates held.

  **§3.9 turnover causes** (decisions.md #027)
  The turnover GATE is untouched — same BASE_TURNOVER, same contest,
  same coach/fatigue scaling — so the turnover COUNT never moves
  (#027 A). A post-declaration weighted draw only picks WHICH of
  nine causes it was, replacing §3.2's binary STOLEN / LOST_BALL.
  STOLEN stays dominant and keeps the pickStealer + recordSteal()
  path; every cause charges the ball-handler. Modest avg-10 leans on
  four causes (#027 C). Note LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS is on TURNOVER
  and must NOT be confused with §3.8's OUT_OF_BOUNDS_* on REBOUND —
  different play types, deliberately distinct vocabulary (#027 D).
  Free by construction → no recalibration.

  **§3.10 rebounding fouls + the team-foul/bonus substrate** (#028)
  A non-shooting foul during the rebound phase, carved off the TOP
  of the board contest and short-circuiting it (C — the §3.7 shape).
  TWO-SIDED (A2): defensive box-out push (dominant) or offensive
  over-the-back, so the committing team is NOT implied by the
  possession orientation — hence game_event.committing_team_id, the
  one additive column this arc took (D). The penalty is **DERIVED**
  from the FOUL log, never stored (A1), emit-then-count so the Nth
  foul awards the bonus itself. Bonus FTs reuse awardFreeThrows
  verbatim (B). NOT free: +2.7 pts before tuning, of which only
  ~1.1 was bonus FTs — **the bigger channel was retained
  possessions**, which the design did not anticipate. BASE_FOUL
  proved the WRONG lever (trimming it RAISES points); the fix was
  the shot BASE_* rates trimmed ~1.2%.

  **§3.11 and-1** (decisions.md #029)
  A defensive foul on a shot that STILL GOES IN: made FG + 1 FT.
  Modeled as a SECOND, post-make foul roll (A1) BESIDE the assist
  (A3) inside SHOT — MADE — the pre-shot foul branch + BASE_FOUL
  are untouched, so the and-1 rate stays independently tunable
  (the §3.7/§3.10 carve, a third time). Scoped to made DRIVE/POST
  (A2 — §3.12 widens to all shot types + fouled-three = 3 FTs).
  Awards exactly ONE FT via a per-situation count through the reused
  awardFreeThrows (B); never forks the possession (the make already
  ended it). Rate = rareEventProbability(AND_ONE_BASE, …,
  AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY) — reuse the machine, own dials, avoiding the
  PROB_FLOOR/global-SENSITIVITY traps §3.7+§3.10 hit (C). Free throws
  become SELF-DESCRIBING (D): each FREE_THROW carries its source
  (SHOOTING / BONUS / AND_ONE), retiring §3.10's accepted ambiguity
  now that there are three FT sources. No schema / OpenAPI / new
  PlayType (AND_ONE is a FOUL outcome, committing_team_id = defTeamId).
  PURE-ADDITIVE points lift → recalibrate the shot BASE_* lever, NOT
  BASE_FOUL (wrong-way, #028 note), by multiple runs to the mean (E).
endlegend

@enduml
